# width: 120
# height: 40
# `Ctrl+Q` with unsaved work raises a box that NAMES what is unsaved and
# offers Save all / Quit anyway / Cancel. Cancel has the focus, so Enter
# on a box you did not mean to raise is safe. Esc cancels, a second
# `Ctrl+Q` quits anyway, and a clean workspace never sees the box.

write one.txt "one\n"
write two.txt "two\n"
open one.txt
open two.txt

# Nothing raised yet. (The clean workspace's own box — Quit / Cancel —
# is `quit_confirm_clean.test`; this file is the unsaved-work one.)
expect screen lacks "Quit mnml?"

type CHANGED
expect dirty true
key ctrl+q
expect screen contains "Quit mnml?"
expect screen contains "Unsaved: two.txt"
expect screen contains "Save all"
expect screen contains "Quit anyway"
expect screen contains "Cancel"

# Esc cancels; the work is still there.
key esc
expect screen lacks "Quit mnml?"
expect dirty true
expect file two.txt lacks "CHANGED"

# Both buffers dirty: the box names both, in pane order.
command buffer.prev
expect pane "one.txt"
type CHANGED
key ctrl+q
expect screen contains "Unsaved: one.txt, two.txt"

# A click on Cancel answers it too. Row 14 is the button row — row 15 is
# the box's bottom border, and a click there dismisses the box like any
# click that misses, so it would have proved nothing.
click 74 14
expect screen lacks "Quit mnml?"
expect dirty true

# The hotkey letters fire their own button: `c` is Cancel.
key ctrl+q
expect screen contains "Quit mnml?"
key c
expect screen lacks "Quit mnml?"
expect dirty true

# The arrows move the focus off Cancel and Enter fires what they land on
# — left once from Cancel is Quit anyway, twice is Save all.
key ctrl+q
key left
key left
key enter
expect screen lacks "Quit mnml?"
expect file one.txt contains "CHANGED"
expect file two.txt contains "CHANGED"
expect dirty false

# (`Quit anyway`, the `q` hotkey and a SECOND `Ctrl+Q` all end the
# session, which this harness cannot assert on — `cmd_app.zig` covers
# all three, and that the on-disk files are untouched.)
